# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Marthe Bideault et al. (2024). Polyvalent machine-learned potential for cobalt: From bulk to nanoparticles.
#   Physical Review Materials. doi:10.1103/physrevmaterials.8.123803  arXiv:2404.02626v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2404.02626v2 (sha256 2a30ec02ad1ba724...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 536 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/bideault2024.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the q-SNAP for Co trained with the MedeA MLPG on
# spin-polarized VASP PBE energies, forces and stresses of unit cells,
# bulk MD, defects, surfaces and nanoparticles (2-308 atoms); training
# and test MAE/RMSE/R2 of Table II. Bulk, surface, thermal and
# nanoparticle results are properties.

